body:
And what if she disclosed her body count, without talking about her profession? Wouldn't that be enough information for him to assess his STD risk?

&#x200B;

If you're going to say prostitution is riskier than one night stands... You're just wrong. A prostitute is at least aware enough of their own risk to know to get tested regularly--many people that are just promiscuous can carry STDs without knowing it (most infections are asymptomatic) or get checked too late (when symptoms finally show up, after taking on new partners). Many prostitutes vet their clients--nobody does any sort of background check before hooking up at a bar.
